  The fixture this class builds, and why its outcome is not inferable from source
    This is the only record in this folder whose fixture reaches the rule engine. The setup method loads a
    real spreadsheet decision table from the classpath, /rules/drools-task-rules.xlsx, asserts that the
    resource exists, compiles it with the spreadsheet compiler, adds it to a knowledge builder as a decision
    table resource, fails the fixture if the builder reports any build error, and only then derives a
    stateless session from the resulting knowledge base. Both tests execute that session against a task
    object. Whether the two pass or fail cannot be read off the source at all: the answer depends on what the
    rule engine and its expression language do with a real spreadsheet at run time. That is the whole reason
    this record asserts no outcome, and the reason the attempt above is reported in full rather than
    summarised.

